[ti:Day 16]

[00:00.00]anti-subsidy 例 The United States will still use traditional trade remedies such as anti-dumping and anti-subsidy laws to correct distortions of trade. 美国将继续运用反倾销和反补贴方案等传 统贸易补救措施来纠正贸易扭曲。
[00:18.31]contour 例 The truly refreshing and unique contour and trapezium design adds a modern touch to your bathroom. 真正令人耳目一新的独特轮廓和梯形 设计给你的浴室增添了现代的格调。
[00:31.24]enhance 例 The practical experience in a large company will enhance your chances of getting a good job. 在大企业实习的经历会增加你找到好 工作的几率。
[00:43.31]trudge 例 We have to trudge through the snow to the bank. 我们不得不在雪中费力地走，一直走到那家 银行。
[00:49.70]user-friendly 例 The system is user-friendly. 此系统很好用。
[00:55.24]immune 例 The employment rate is not immune to economic recession. 就业率不可能不受到经济 衰退的影响。
[01:03.05]horizon 例 Reading broadens your horizons, giving you access to new perspectives and ideas. 阅读可 以开阔你的视野，帮助你接触到新的观点和思 想。
[01:13.98]blossom 例 The industry can blossom over night if you find an outlet for new products. 如果你能为新 产品找到出路，这个产业在一夜之间就能兴旺起 来。
[01:23.92]crucial 例 With the right products and the right terms, these workers can still have access to that crucial crutch. 拥有合适的产品和合适的条款， 这些工人仍然可以得到这些重要的支柱。
[01:37.41]finish 例 The 17-year affiliation between Liverpool and Carlsberg will finish at the end of the current season. 利物浦和嘉士伯啤酒公司之间17 年的合作关系将于本赛季结束后终止。
[01:50.62]cordial 例 The two sides exchanged in-depth opinions on bilateral relations and other issues of common concern in a cordial and friendly atmosphere. 双方在亲切友好的气氛中就双边关 系和其他共同关心的问题深入交换了意见。
[02:08.37]distribution 例 The upcoming conference will discuss the fair distribution of wealth and income. 即将召 开的会议将要讨论财富和收入的公平分配问题。
[02:20.02]confer 例 The new corporate leaders often fly to Washington to confer with government officials on national policy. 这些新的公司领导人 常常飞往华盛顿，同政府官员商讨国家政策。
[02:33.79]impede 例 Don't impede your career development with these trivial things. 不要让这些琐事阻碍你事业 的发展。
[02:42.60]tally 例 The bag I have received does not tally with the sample on-line. 我收到的包与网上的样品不 相吻合。
[02:50.83]alongside 例 Alongside an explanation of the sources of firm differentials, there must also be an explanation of the mechanism. 在对企业差异来 源进行解释之外，还应该对机制进行解释。
[03:06.03]quantum 例 He provided everyone with the same quantum of free gifts. 他给每个人分发了等量的 赠品。
[03:13.98]divulge 例 None of those clearinghouses would divulge the members of their risk committees. 这几家清算所没有一家愿意透露风险管理委员会 的成员。
[03:24.92]automate 例 There are some great products out there that can automate this process. 现在市场上已 经有一些不错的产品可以使这个过程自动化。
[03:34.72]define 例 It is urgent for the government to define its trade relationship with the European Union clearly. 政府迫切需要清晰地定义其和欧盟之间的 贸易关系。
[03:47.36]collide 例 We know that more is to be gained when great powers cooperate than when they collide. 我们知道，大国之间只有通过合作而非冲 突才能获得更大的收益。
[03:58.43]coalition 例 The coalition government sees this as a way of delegating power and strengthening localism. 联合政府将此视为一条权力下放和加强 地区化的道路。
[04:10.93]scupper 例 They worry that the new demands might scupper the whole deal. 他们担心这些新的要求 可能会毁了整个交易。
[04:19.31]overhaul 例 It is general ly appreciated that the government plans to overhaul financial regulations this year. 众所周知，政府计划今年 对金融法规进行全面改革。
[04:32.66]endorse 例 The cheque is endorsed. 该支票已背书。
[04:36.63]boutique 例 The company now lets you add the number of whatever you want at their new online boutique. 在此公司新开的网上精品店中，你可以 随意增加任何你想要的物品的数量。
[04:48.42]bond 例 Issuing more government bonds is an expansionary monetary policy. 发行更多的国债 属于扩张性货币政策。
[04:57.23]demanding 例 The job he introduced to me is much too demanding for me. 对我来说，他介绍的这份工 作要求太高了。
[05:05.18]convince 例 How can I convince my boss to invest in our ideas? 我怎样才能说服我的老板投资我们的 新创意呢？
[05:12.14]autonomous 例 Each team should be autonomous except in matters affecting other teams or the organisation as a whole. 除了涉及其他团队或整 个组织的相关事宜，每个团队都应该实行自治。
[05:25.91]overwhelm 例 The country fears that giant multinational firms will overwhelm its domestic enterprises. 这个国家担心大型跨国企业会击垮国内企业。
[05:38.41]clipboard 例 In a series of experiments, study participants were asked to answer questionnaires that were attached to a metal clipboard. 在一系列实验中，研究对象被要求填
[05:54.74]eloquent 例 The chief negotiator is tough and eloquent. 主讲人有很好的口才，是个难对付的人。
[06:01.27]outlay 例 A monthly outlay on the health sector is budgeted at two million dollars. 每月卫生领域 的预算经费是200万美元。
[06:10.93]authentic 例 The young customers are inclined to buy authentic products. 年轻的消费者倾向于购买正 宗的产品。
[06:19.59]appraise 例 How would your present employer appraise you? 你现在的老板会怎样评价你呢？
[06:26.41]craft 例 A college adviser is giving a weekend tutorial on how to craft a well-rounded extracurricular portfolio. 一位大学指导老师开了 个周末辅导班，指导如何精巧地制作一份全面的 个人课外活动资料。
[06:39.90]epitomise 例 The meeting record epitomises all the topics we discussed. 会议记录概括了讨论过的 所有论题。
[06:48.42]regroup 例 Give them time and they will recover, regroup and come up with a new strategy. 给 他们时间，他们会恢复元气，继而重组并想出新 的策略。
[06:58.65]canteen 例 The billionaire was determined to have lunch in the in-house canteen at his company. 这位亿万富翁决定在他公司内部的自助食堂吃午 饭。
[07:09.86]eschew 例 You'd better eschew junk food. 最好远离垃 圾食品。
[07:14.55]escalate 例 The real estate price war is escalating. 房地 产的价格战在不断升级。
[07:20.66]hypocrisy 例 The growing protectionist sentiment in the US is particularly noisome because it reeks of so much hypocrisy. 正在美国滋生的保护主义情 绪是极端有害的，因为其中掺杂着太多伪善。
[07:35.14]appalling 例 Everyone could not help but notice the absolutely appalling physical conditions and the oppressive atmosphere. 每个人都不由自主 地注意到了可怕的环境和令人窒息的氛围。
[07:50.19]gilt-edged 例 The inflation-linked bonds are among the gilt-edged ones, and are often regarded as risk-free. 通胀保值国债属于金边债券，通常被认 为是没有风险的。
[08:03.26]expenditure 例 As for an international company, the business travel is a big part of the overhead expenditure. 对跨国公司来说，差旅费在总开支 中占很大比例。
[08:16.32]envision 例 We envision our company has a great future. 我们预想公司的未来一片光明。
[08:22.71]outsource 例 They decided to outsource some projects to other small companies for financial reasons. 由于资金问题，他们决定将一些项目外 包给其他小公司。
[08:34.79]amortisation 例 Free cash flow is a broader measure that takes earnings and adds depreciation and amortisation while subtracting capital expenditures. 自由现金流是一种更广泛的衡量指 标，等于企业获利加上折旧和摊销，同时扣除资 本支出。
[08:53.10]offer 例 All of this merchandise is on offer. 所有这些
[08:58.22]consensus 例 The whole of society should arrive at the consensus that wealth is not the hallmark of social status, but individual virtues and ethics are. 整个社会应该达成共识，即财富不应该是社 会地位的标志，真正的标志应该是品质和道德。
[09:16.25]mock 例 Dedicate one day prior to the interview to a mock Q&A. 在面试前事先拿出一天来模拟问答环 节。
[09:23.21]muddle 例 Tell me the truth and don't muddle me around! 把实情告诉我，别对我敷衍了事！
[09:29.46]facelift 例 The building projects are not just a way of giving the city a facelift; they also keep people in work. 这些建筑项目并非仅仅是给这个城市做 个“整容手术”，它们还为人们创造工作机会
[09:42.52]dubious 例 Those figures alone are a dubious basis for such a conclusion. 仅凭那些数据就得出这种结 论并不可靠。
